course: dictionary
lesson: 12998
title: Showing feelings and forms
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Expressed is the past form of the verb express. To express something means to show or say what you feel or think. «Mia expressed her sadness by sitting quietly by the window.» Mia did not have to say it. Her quiet sitting showed how sad she was.
explain: You can express a feeling in words, in a look or in an action. «Tom expressed his thanks with a big smile.» The smile shows the thanks, so the word fits the action as well as speech.
explain: In maths, expressed means written in a certain form. «Give the answer expressed as a fraction.» So you write one half, not 0.5. Check your meaning: swap in «shown» or «written» and see if the sentence still makes sense.
fact: Express is a verb, and expressed is its past form, used for something that has already happened.
fact: «Expressed» can mean said or shown in words, looks or actions.
fact: In maths, «expressed as» means written in a certain form, such as a fraction, a decimal or with a unit.
fact: As an adjective, «expressed» means clearly stated, not just hinted at: «an expressed wish».
fact: Phrases you may meet are «expressed concern», «expressed in centimetres» and «expressed as a percentage».
exercise: «Mia expressed her sadness by sitting quietly by the window.» What does expressed mean here? | Forgot | Hid | *Showed | Lost
exercise: «Give the answer expressed as a fraction.» What does expressed as mean here? | Rounded up to a whole number | *Written in the form of | Copied from the board | Spoken aloud by the teacher
exercise: «Tom expressed his thanks with a big smile.» How did Tom express his thanks? | By going to sleep | *With a big smile | By running out of the room | By writing a long letter
test: «The length was expressed in centimetres.» What does expressed in mean here? | *Written using the unit centimetres | Drawn in bright colours | Hidden under a book | Sung loudly to the class
test: «Her worry was expressed in her quiet voice and her frown.» What does expressed mean here? | Repeated many times | Hidden | Forgotten | *Shown
exam: Which sentence uses expressed as an adjective, meaning clearly stated? | The bird expressed its wings in the sky. | He expressed his dinner onto the plate. | We expressed the bus at noon. | *Her expressed wish was to visit the zoo.
